# LeakSanitizer suppressions — third-party only. Nothing in keyward belongs here;
# if one of our own frames shows up in a leak report, fix the leak.
#
# libsecret allocates a SecretPrompt (via g_initable_new) when it tries to unlock
# a locked collection, and leaks it when no prompter can be reached — which is
# exactly the headless situation SecretServiceLocked.Isolated creates on purpose.
# 8 bytes, once, inside libsecret; not reachable or fixable from our side.
#
#   #6 _secret_prompt_instance (libsecret-1.so.0)
leak:_secret_prompt_instance
